      "text_content": "# Questionnaire Actions — verification and fixes\n\n**Scope updated following product clarification:** Per-repeat notes (QA-16), search by code (QA-25), and facility-level Actions (QA-36) are excluded from this release. The search-by-code frontend change and its test were removed. The import concern (QA-22) is choosing a slug before creating an imported questionnaire, not enabling general slug editing. Patient standalone Actions (QA-40) are intentionally unsupported; the frontend now stops offering/listing them. Earlier backend-work recommendations for these items are superseded. Slack material remains outside the repository and is not PR content.\n\nReviewed all **43 indexed reports** from the complete channel archive. Work is on frontend branch `bodhi/questionnaire-actions`, based on `d45cdd0b6`, as uncommitted changes. Backend source was inspected only; its pre-existing changes were preserved.\n\nThe current scope addresses 31 frontend items and the frontend portions of 2 additional items. Three items are explicitly excluded: per-repeat notes, search by code, and facility-level Actions. Three items retain backend/workflow dependencies (questionnaire audit timestamps, manual execution, and cross-facility draft validation). Three items were already implemented/addressed, and three product questions were explained without changing their current behavior.\n\nRuntime assertions and source review are distinct: targeted browser checks cover the major flows; minor presentation changes were reviewed in source and against the archived screenshots. This is not a claim that every original screenshot was independently reproduced.\n\n## Current-scope validation\n\n- 228 unit tests passed (43 suites).\n- 21 focused production-browser checks passed in this follow-up: 7 Actions checks and 14 import/authoring/access/navigation checks.\n- TypeScript and production build passed. Changed-file formatting/lint passed with 0 errors and 18 existing warnings; diff whitespace check is clean.\n- No Slack/transcript/report artifacts or context-specific test names are in the repository changes. External working reports remain outside the repository. Pre-existing `.gstack/` logs are unrelated and must not be included in a PR.\n\n## Earlier validation checkpoint\n\n- **222 unit tests passed** across 42 suites.\n- **26 distinct Playwright browser checks passed**, using the production build and local backend. The first pass had 15 passes; corrected tests and added integration checks contributed 10 further distinct passes; the final studio check passed separately. All initially failing selected checks passed after test locator/fixture updates.\n- **TypeScript and production build passed**, with `REACT_CARE_API_URL=http://localhost:9000`.\n- Changed-file **Prettier and ESLint completed: 0 errors, 18 existing warnings**. `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Tests used local admin authentication. Other saved role sessions could not refresh, so this was not a full cross-role permissions audit. No database snapshot was restored.\n- No backend patch, deployed-backend mutation, or Slack reply was made.\n\nThe 26 browser checks cover instruction search/grouping/compatibility, expression restoration and syntax placement, typed patient values, Action configuration create/edit/delete, question editing and numeric operators, choice layout, studio issues/discard/search, organization staging and save recovery, Draft creation, required markers, disabled history controls, both questionnaire pickers, location response correction/persistence, ValueSet create/preview, starred code search, header search, and desktop/admin sidebar behavior.\n\nRaw validation logs are in [validation](validation/). Presentation-only details without dedicated browser assertions retain source/screenshot evidence in the per-report reviews.\n\n## Per-report disposition\n\n| ID / report | Outcome | Finding or change | Slack source |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| QA-01 — Questionnaire selector. | Already present | Shared searchable popover on desktop and drawer on mobile; retained. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788944434452619) |\n| QA-02 — Organisation save behavior. | Fixed | Organization changes are staged and saved with questionnaire metadata in one atomic batch. Selection objects survive add/remove/re-add; save-state regressions cover failed saves and pending edits. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788945082940799) |\n| QA-03 — Inline heading editing. | Fixed | Canvas question and group headings can be edited inline. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788945304634699) |\n| QA-04 — Numeric enable-when operators. | Fixed | Integer and decimal conditions offer Equals and Not Equals. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788945867865699) |\n| QA-05 — Exist enable-when operator. | Fixed | Answerable question types offer presence/absence conditions. Non-answering group/display nodes remain excluded. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788945867865699) |\n| QA-06 — Collapsed sidebar styling. | Already addressed in current code | The fullscreen studio excludes the application sidebar. Current sidebar preview behavior also has browser coverage; the old screenshot layout was not reproduced. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788946142666419) |\n| QA-07 — Answer-type search border. | Fixed | Removed the extra search-input border/ring within the answer-type popover. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788946498947029) |\n| QA-08 — Subquestion editing context. | Fixed | Inspector identifies the immediate parent of a subquestion or subgroup. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788947147986069) |\n| QA-09 — Instruction search. | Fixed | Instructions are searchable. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788950490823469) |\n| QA-10 — Conditional required marker. | Fixed | Action-referenced questions show required markers and accessible required state, using the same extractor as submit validation. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788950661189759) |\n| QA-11 — Expression error placement. | Fixed | Expression syntax errors render immediately below the input. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788951458047739) |\n| QA-12 — Restore valid conditions. | Fixed | Returning from an invalid expression restores the last valid condition state. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788951458047739) |\n| QA-13 — Small-screen structure dropdown. | Fixed | Answer/structure picker height and width respect available viewport space; the list scrolls. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788952079447199) |\n| QA-14 — Location response error status. | Fixed | Resource responses offer confirmed Mark as entered in error using the existing endpoint, preserving answers and refreshing the viewer. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788952397380699) |\n| QA-15 — Location questionnaire button. | Explained; retained | Screenshot highlights the Newest first ordering label and Refresh control. The latter reloads responses. No replacement behavior was requested. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1788952567755419) |\n| QA-16 — Notes for repeatable items. | Excluded by product scope | No per-repeat note changes are included. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1789024906284809) |\n| QA-17 — Subquestion row layout. | Fixed | Subquestion titles truncate and action buttons remain on the same row. | [Report](https://rebuildearth.slack.com/archives/C0C1DB92YHE/p1789025781112759) |\n| QA-18 — Read-only structured-question history. | Fixed | All four structured-question history import controls ho